  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="4ac7a1c7-be83-5b68-a633-3357faa1dd48" activityNameId="3cd56403-fb85-5c51-af84-5f4ed19456aa" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Natural gas, production DZ, at long-distance pipeline</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Natural gas, production DZ, at long-distance pipeline
In 2019 58% of the imported Algerian natural gas to RER was imported by pipeline and 42% as LNG. An average distance of 1180 km is estimated for the pipeline export from Algeria, of which are 130 km offshore pipeline. The estimated shipping distance for LNG are 11700 km.;
f6dd9d94-174b-328c-a91d-7ceb39b37f26
This dataset describes the transport needed for an average export of Algerian natural gas. Gas losses and emissions during seasonal storage are included.
Location:  The data for storage emissions are based on global data. The amount of gas stored is a rough estimate based on European data. The average weighted transport distance is based on the trade movements 2019.
Technology: The distance is an European average based on the European long-distance pipeline network and LNG shipping routes.
Time period: Transport modes investigated for 2019.
Production volume: none
Sampling: Literature. Online calculators for distances.
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_f6dd9d94-174b-328c-a91d-7ceb39b37f26.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
